{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.brings_euler_characteristic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.brings_euler_characteristic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.quantum_dimension_recovers_chi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.quantum_dimension_recovers_chi","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_euler_characteristic.lean#L206-L225","doc":"**Substrate recovery** — the .md's final clause: the quantum\ndimension of `A = 𝒪_q(SU(2))` specialised at the Descartes substrate\nparameter `q₀` (the categorical trace `tr(id_A)`, modelled by\n`categoricalTrace`) recovers the categorical Euler characteristic\n`χ(A) = −6`, viewed in the ground ring `R`.\n\nFully derived (no `sorry`): both sides evaluate to `−6` —\n`categoricalTrace` by `categorical_trace_eq_neg_six` (from the\n`q`-family super-trace), and `χ(A)` by `brings_euler_characteristic`.\nNo upstream value-assumption and no axiom are used; the only inputs\nare the surface's Betti numbers `(1, 2g, 1)`, `dim_q 𝟙 = 1`, and the\ngenus `g = 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.categorical_trace_eq_neg_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.categorical_trace_eq_neg_six","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_euler_characteristic.lean#L192-L204","doc":"**Trace of the identity = −6** ([`lem:brings-euler-characteristic`]):\nthe categorical trace `tr(id_A)` (the super-trace `categoricalTrace`)\nof `A = 𝒪_q(SU(2))` over `Σ₄` equals `χ(Σ₄) = −6`.\n\nDerived from the super-trace over the cohomology\n(`categorical_trace_eq_euler`) plus the genus fact `g = 4` — never\nread back from a class field asserting `−6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.categorical_trace_q_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.categorical_trace_q_independent","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_euler_characteristic.lean#L180-L190","doc":"**`q`-independence**: the categorical trace does not depend on the\ndeformation parameter.  The substrate evaluation at `q₀` is therefore\nnot a fit — the `q`-dependence cancels because the cohomology modules\nare quantum-trivial and the alternating sum returns the classical\nEuler characteristic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.categorical_trace_eq_euler","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.categorical_trace_eq_euler","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_euler_characteristic.lean#L167-L178","doc":"**Trace of the identity = Euler formula** (`q`-family super-trace):\nthe categorical trace `tr(id_A)(q)`, the super-trace of quantum\ndimensions over `H^*(Σ_g)`, equals `2 − 2g` for **every** `q`.\n\nDerived, not assumed: `dim_q 𝟙 = 1` (`qdimUnit`, the `q`-family\nconstant) reduces the super-trace to the alternating Betti sum\n`1 − 2g + 1 = 2 − 2g` by `ring`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.brings_euler_characteristic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.brings_euler_characteristic","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_euler_characteristic.lean#L150-L165","doc":"**Lemma** ([`lem:brings-euler-characteristic`]):\non Bring's surface, `g = 4`, the Euler characteristic obeys the\nEuler formula `χ(A) = 2 − 2g`, and its value is `χ(A) = −6`.\n\nThe first conjunct is the geometric input; the second is the\ndefinition of `chi_A`; the third is **derived** by `norm_num`\nafter substituting `g = 4`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:brings-euler-characteristic","label":"lem:brings-euler-characteristic","md":"quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-euler-characteristic.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsEulerCharacteristicContext.categoricalTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsEulerCharacteristicContext.categoricalTrace","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_euler_characteristic.lean#L133-L144","doc":"The categorical trace of the identity `tr(id_A)`, computed as the\n**super-trace** (alternating sum) of the quantum dimensions of the\ncohomology `H^i(Σ_g)`:\n\n`tr(id_A)(q) = b₀·dim_q𝟙 − b₁·dim_q𝟙 + b₂·dim_q𝟙`,\n\nwith Betti numbers `(b₀, b₁, b₂) = (1, 2g, 1)` of the closed\norientable genus-`g` surface.  Because each `H^i` is quantum-trivial\n(`qdimUnit`), this evaluates to the alternating Betti sum for all\n`q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsEulerCharacteristicContext.qdimUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsEulerCharacteristicContext.qdimUnit","kind":"def","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_euler_characteristic.lean#L124-L131","doc":"Quantum dimension of the monoidal unit, `dim_q 𝟙 = tr_q(id_𝟙)`, as\na function of the deformation parameter `q`.  Categorically this is\n`1 ∈ End(𝟙) ≅ R` for **every** `q`, so the `q`-family is the\nconstant function `1`.  It is the only `q`-datum the recovery needs:\nthe cohomology `H^i(Σ₄)` are trivial (quantum-dimension-`1`)\n`Rep(SU_q(2))`-modules, so `dim_q H^i = b_i · dim_q 𝟙 = b_i` at\nevery `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsEulerCharacteristicContext.chi_A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsEulerCharacteristicContext.chi_A","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_euler_characteristic.lean#L118-L122","doc":"The categorical Euler characteristic, **defined** by the Euler\nformula `χ = 2 − 2g`.  An integer topological invariant (`ℤ`, not\nthe archimedean `ℝ`), embedded into the ground ring `R` where the\ncategorical trace lives (see `quantum_dimension_recovers_chi`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsEulerCharacteristicContext.genus_is_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsEulerCharacteristicContext.genus_is_four","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_euler_characteristic.lean#L112-L112","doc":"The classical genus fact for Bring's surface. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsEulerCharacteristicContext.g","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsEulerCharacteristicContext.g","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_euler_characteristic.lean#L110-L110","doc":"Bring's surface genus — the genuine geometric input `g(Σ₄) = 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsEulerCharacteristicContext.q0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsEulerCharacteristicContext.q0","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_euler_characteristic.lean#L108-L108","doc":"The Descartes substrate parameter `q₀`, at which the quantum\ndimension is specialised.  A ground-ring element (`R`, generic per\n§7c); its archimedean value `q₀ ≈ 1.1097 ∈ ℝ` is the downstream\n`R := ℝ` evaluation, not performed here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsEulerCharacteristicContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsEulerCharacteristicContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_euler_characteristic.lean#L103-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsEulerCharacteristicContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.BringsEulerCharacteristicContext","kind":"class","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/brings_euler_characteristic.lean#L96-L112","doc":"Geometric context for the Euler-characteristic lemma, over a\ngeneric ground ring `R = End(𝟙)`.\n\nThe geometric datum is the genus of Bring's surface, `g(Σ₄) = 4`;\nthe Betti numbers `(1, 2g, 1)` and the Euler characteristic are\nderived from it, so the lemma's value is computed rather than\nassumed. ","signatureChunk":0}]}